        {
          "id": 1248243509,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Perhaps just get rid of the SUSE version check and continue to use cmake install for RedHat and Fedora?\n\nWe can probably assume that RedHat 7 and earlier aren't being used on the 4.0 branch and later. (Theoretically someone might have built their own updated RPMs for all our support libraries, and tried to use our spec file, I suppose.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
